# GitHub Actions repository variables used by .github/workflows/build.yml and test-and-lint.yml.
# These are settings, not secrets: GitHub hides secret values, so a secret could not be used here.
#
# Where to add them: GitHub repository > Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions >
# Variables tab > New repository variable. Use the names below exactly.
# Or copy this file to .env.variables, fill it in, and upload every entry at once with:
#   gh variable set -f .env.variables
#
# Every entry is optional; leave it unset to keep the default it describes.

# Self-hosted Mac

# A label of your own Mac registered as a self-hosted runner (Settings > Actions > Runners >
# New self-hosted runner). GitHub gives every self-hosted Mac the label macOS; a custom
# label added when registering it works too. When set, the macOS desktop, iOS and App Store
# Connect jobs and the macOS desktop startup test run on that Mac; leave it unset to use GitHub's
# macOS runner from release.runners.mac in product.conf.json. An Apple silicon Mac needs Rosetta
# (softwareupdate --install-rosetta --agree-to-license): the release check starts the x64 app.
MAC_SELF_HOSTED_RUNNER=
